  "name": "Three-bay, four-storey frame",
  "engineer": "",
  "description": "Illustrative unbraced steel moment frame, not a structural design. Three 6 m bays and four 3.5 m storeys (18 m wide × 14 m high); four fixed bases and rigid joints. Downward beam loads: 10 kN/m at levels 1–3 and 7.5 kN/m at the roof, plus member self-weight. Global +X floor loads: 8, 12, 16 and 20 kN at the left column, bottom to top. Idealised welded I-sections (depth × flange width × web × flange thickness, mm): columns 400 × 300 × 12 × 20; beams 350 × 180 × 10 × 16. E = 210000 MPa; density = 7850 kg/m³. No code-derived loads, buckling or second-order checks.",
